text.section:
Disability benefit payments shall be offset by an amount equal to any sums payable to a participating employee from the following sources:

During the first 12 months the employee receives disability benefits, an amount equal to the employee's wages and salary from any employment multiplied by the creditable compensation replacement percentage;


After the first 12 months the employee receives disability benefits, an amount equal to 70 percent of the employee's wages and salary from any employment;


Disability payments from the Social Security Administration, local government disability benefits, federal civil service disability benefits, or other similar governmental disability program benefits received by the employee or his family as a result of the qualifying disability;


Benefits received from any other group insurance contract provided to the participating employee by his employer for the purpose of providing income replacement; and


Benefits paid under any compulsory benefits law.
